hi there  today i want to talk a little bit about  time you know i often say that there's  three elements in language learning it's  there's your attitude there's the time  with the language and then  being attentive  and that three kind of are interrelated  i mean the more the  more positive the attitude the more time  you spend the more time you spend the  more you notice the more you notice the  more you get motivated the more you're  motivated  but i think one of the key elements is  time where do we find the time how do we  make the time  you have to develop habits and when you  have habits where you start finding the  time  that improves your attitude improves  your ability to notice so time is kind  of a key element  and a lot of people say i have no time  so i i think we have to look at ways  that we can create time and there's two  things that i would say very quickly  before i get into some of the sort of  where i was today kind of thing  number one obviously wherever you can  listen listen so whether it be like  yesterday i went skiing  uh you know it was a half an hour up  there half an hour back that's an hour i  skied for an hour and a half cross  country skiing and there's three and a  half hours  what'd i say two and a half hours at any  rate  it all adds up if you can listen in the  car and so forth it all adds up  um  the other thing that i've started doing  and i can't really show it to you but i  have a little app here  on my computer  my computer on my iphone  but you can also put on your computer  and it's called a tracker and so every  time i start to listen or read or  something i start it and then when i'm  finished i stop it and what it does it  it forces me to stay on task because  i've started this listening thing i  don't want to be interrupted i've  started reading i won't go and do my  email  so these are different ways because when  you're in a classroom the teacher kind  of forces you to do stuff when you're  studying on your own it's more difficult  to have the discipline to really make  sure that you either find the time or  make the time at any rate today  i would play hockey again this morning  and then i went and drove out to a  korean mall  to have lunch  and us i was going to visit my bookstore  because there's a very nice lady there  but unfortunately i walked in the  bookstore and there was this guy with  his l.a cat pulled down over his head  still wearing his  outdoor jacket looked very un  welcoming korean guy i guess and i said  he's not going to talk to me in korean  and so i uh left and i will go back to  that bookstore when the nice lady is  there  and uh so enjoy the rest of the video is  over people are coming down  off the mountain  and uh  slowly getting darker so i'm gonna head  home this is where the downhill area is  not too much snow this year  normally we'll have three four meters of  snow  uh then we turn around  there's of course you know the parking  lot and so forth it's known as cypress  bowl because there's lots of cypress  trees here uh it's hard to make out what  it is right now and  here of course off in the distance  above the clouds  you can just see the sun  setting it's around 4 30 or so i think  which is getting close to sunset here  and some people are going into the trail  again  i am at the korean mall  um gonna have a korean lunch and then  there's a bookstore here which i'm gonna  visit  maybe chat up the lady in the bookstore  in my limited korean  but all the shops here are korean  uh even i might just go to this uh  restaurant here i'm walking backwards  hope i don't hit a car  this restaurant advertises itself as  well i'll show you on a separate video  inside this uh korean restaurant i  ordered salon  which is some kind of a beef soup  those gentlemen are speaking chinese i  don't know if i'm gonna go over and  bother them or not  but uh here we have it  we'll see what my korean food tastes  like  um  um  you know you got to get into it this  this broth is delicious  the kimchi is excellent absolutely  delicious a little bit of rice here  and what's typical of the korean food of  course is the metal chopsticks  and that kind of gets me in the mood  restaurant  um  um  now i gotta rush off and study some  korean  been charging around and i've been  making this video and editing it  and i'm running out of time so but i  want to ask you people out there how do  you find the time how do you make the  time how much time do you have for your  language learning how do you fit it in  let's get some comments and ideas on  what we can do to find more time

